; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Sine Waves
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     sine, graph, setxy, waves, axes
; SUMMARY:  Plots a sine wave across the screen, then a faster one and a smaller one, and finally adds two waves together.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The turtle moves from left to right. At each step its height is
;   worked out with SIN, so it rises and falls in a smooth wave.
;   Four waves are drawn on a pair of axes: a plain wave, one that
;   wiggles three times as fast, a small one, and the sum of the
;   first two, which looks like a wave with a bumpy back.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the inputs to WAVE: how tall it is, how many
;   times it wiggles across the screen, and its color.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * SIN gives a number between -1 and 1 that goes up and down
;   * SETXY to plot a graph point by point
;   * FOR with a step size to move along the x axis
;   * adding two waves together, point by point
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Use COS instead of SIN. What changes?
;   * Make a wave whose height shrinks as x grows.
;   * Add three waves together. Can you make something like a square wave?
; ============================================================

; Axes: a line across and a line up the middle, with a little label.
to axes
  setpencolor [180 180 190] setpensize 1
  penup setxy -380 0 pendown setxy 380 0
  penup setxy 0 -280 pendown setxy 0 280
  penup setxy 345 -18 label "x
end

; x runs from -360 to 360. :waves full wiggles fit across that width,
; so the angle we give SIN is x times :waves / 2.
to wave :height :waves :color
  setpencolor :color setpensize 3
  penup
  for [x -360 360 3] [
    setxy :x :height * sin :x * :waves / 2
    pendown
  ]
end

; Two waves added together: the height is the sum of both heights.
to sumwave :h1 :w1 :h2 :w2 :color
  setpencolor :color setpensize 3
  penup
  for [x -360 360 3] [
    setxy :x (:h1 * sin :x * :w1 / 2) + (:h2 * sin :x * :w2 / 2)
    pendown
  ]
end

to key :y :color :text
  penup setxy -370 :y setpencolor :color label :text
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [252 252 248]
axes
wave 150 2 [40 110 220]
wave 60 6 [230 120 30]
wave 40 2 [60 170 90]
sumwave 150 2 60 6 [200 40 80]
setlabelheight 15
key 270 [40 110 220] [blue: a tall, slow wave]
key 250 [230 120 30] [orange: three times as fast]
key 230 [60 170 90] [green: small and slow]
key 210 [200 40 80] [red: blue + orange]
